          [
            "internal",
            "The crates' include patterns are anchored with /, so a file of the same name deeper in a crate can never be packaged by accident; each package's contents are unchanged."
          ],
          [
            "fixed",
            "The release's signed security record gives cargo deny's summary. 0.1.2's record gave a fragment of a cargo deny warning in its place, through a pubrel bug since fixed; the check itself passed."
          ],
          [
            "fixed",
            "SUPPLY-CHAIN.md lists every dependency built for any target. It omitted libc and fiat-crypto, which are built only on some targets and were already vetted, and libc's exemption now records its evidence."
